<title>BELGIUM: EU to probe Tesco Irish acquisition.</title>
<headline>EU to probe Tesco Irish acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Thursday it was opening a routine probe into plans by British supermarket chain Tesco Plc to acquire Ireland's biggest grocery chain, Quinnsworth, from Associated British foods.</p>
<p>The move is in line with European Union merger rules which ban the creation or strengthening of dominant position.</p>
<p>Britain's biggest supermarket group Tesco said this month it would pay Associated British Foods (ABF) 630 million pounds to take control of 75 Quinnsworth and Crazy Prices stores in Ireland as well as 34 stores in Northern Ireland trading as Stewarts, Crazy Prices, Superdeal, Westside Stores and Bloomfield, plus a processing business, an off-licence chain and a sports shop group.</p>
<p>The Commission has about a month to approve the deal or start a full probe.</p>
